      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The §3Presses§r are machines that can be used to make §6Plates§r, §6Wires§r, §6Circuits§r, §6Bullet Casings§r as well as §6Compressing§r non-smeltable powders back into their normal form. The burner press burns solid fuel like coal to run.\n\nEvery press operation needs a §6Stamp§r in the top slot. Stamps start out as §6Flat Stamps§r, which are turned into §6Plate§r, §6Wire§r or §6Circuit Stamps§r of the same material on an §3Anvil§r. Stone and iron stamps can be converted on the basic anvil, steel, titanium and obsidian stamps need the steel anvil.\n\nStamps lose durability with every use. Stone stamps break very quickly and are only worth it for your first few plates, iron stamps are the sensible starting point, and steel or obsidian stamps last much longer. Keep a spare stamp next to the press: a broken stamp silently stops an automated line.\n\n§2A preheater can be placed next to the Burner Press to increase its speed.",
